# agent_stall_test is the stream-stall recovery suite (specs/043-llm-stream-
# stall-recovery — T011 large test, plus specs/044-llm-stall-recovery-fix
# T011 cases b/c/d), run against the stall deploy
# (deploy_agent_stall.yaml — selects the agent_timeouts config block
# (streamIdleTimeoutMs=5000, toolHeartbeatIntervalMs=2000) via the 045
# deploy-config channel; config values bypass the env channel's 60s clamp
# by design):
#   - TestAgentStallRecoveryWithQueuedMessage (043 US1/US2, quickstart
#     Scenario 5): a fake-llm turn that emits its reasoning delta then
#     stops with the connection alive (sample_stall.yaml) is detected
#     within the idle window — warn + wait emitted, the queued message
#     RETAINED (no QueueSignal(0), FR-006) and delivered on the next turn
#     (FR-007).
#   - TestAgentStallToolExecutionNotFalselyDetected (043 US3, Scenario 6):
#     a saolei_operate dispatch delayed 12s (> idleTimeout — ~6 heartbeat
#     ticks at the 2s cadence) on the production saolei MCP path does not
#     false-stall — the client-side heartbeat wrapper keeps the idle timer
#     alive (FR-003/SC-003).
#   - TestAgentStallDetectedWithinConfiguredWindow (044 US1 regression,
#     FR-001/SC-004): a real silent dropout is still detected within the
#     config-driven 5s window — elapsed detection bracketed against the
#     older windows (15s/30s/60s) and the 120s default.
#   - TestAgentStallPersistsPartialOutput (044 US3, FR-004/FR-005/
#     SC-002/SC-003): after the stalled turn terminates, ListMessages
#     returns the already-streamed reasoning partial with
#     completion = PART_COMPLETION_INTERRUPTED on the tail part.
#   - TestAgentStallThinkInterruptGapDetected (046→044 enabler pair,
#     quickstart D3): a think-interrupt-gap turn streams two reasoning
#     chunks then a finite 15s gap; the gap exceeds the config-driven 5s
#     window so the detector fires mid-thinking at ~5s; the pre-gap
#     chunks persist as the partial output with
#     completion = PART_COMPLETION_INTERRUPTED on the tail part
#     (specs/046-fake-llm-think-chunking/contracts/template-config.md
#     §3.3).
#
# size = medium: at the config-driven 5s/2s timings the five cases'
# healthy paths total ~60–85s (T012's "<2min" planning upper bound), so
# medium's 300s budget leaves ≥3.5× CI headroom — small's 60s is
# insufficient since the suite itself exceeds 60s (style/large_test.md
# §测试用例: size per actual need; size→timeout mapping small=60s /
# medium=300s / large=900s per bazel test.size, and `guitar run` executes
# via `bazel test --config=largetest`, whose .bazelrc only sets
# --cache_test_results=no — size is the effective hard timeout). Under
# the worst designed failure — a config-channel regression to the 120s
# default — T2 passes (~25s), T5 fails fast (~17s, the 15s gap
# under-runs the 120s window so the turn completes and its warn/bracket
# assertions fire), and T1/T3/T4 are bounded by the 75s wsReadTimeout
# read deadline (the stall wait aborts before the 120s detection could
# fire) — every failure path stays well under the 300s budget.
go_largetest(
    name = "agent_stall_test",
    size = "medium",
    srcs = [
        "agent_stall_test.go",
        "helpers_test.go",
        "saolei_fixtures_test.go",
    ],
    embedsrcs = SAOLEI_EMBEDSRCS,
    deps = [
        "//common/gopkg/testtool",
        "//projects/game",
        "//projects/game/pkg/gameconst",
        TRACECONTEXT_DEP,
        "@com_github_gorilla_websocket//:websocket",
        "@org_golang_google_protobuf//encoding/protojson",
        "@org_golang_google_protobuf//proto",
    ],
)
